Two new options have been added to the Settings menu's Chat section, allowing players to have permanently banned and permanently muted accounts removed from their Ignore lists.

The option for removing banned accounts is enabled by default, whereas the option for removing muted accounts is disabled by default. The check runs quietly once per day, rather than checking continually, so as to avoid excessive load on the chat system.

We've also got a few smaller changes to finish:
* Party leaders in Tombs of Amascut can now promote other members of the party while the group is forming in the lobby.
* It's no longer possible to redeem a Bond in the last three minutes before a server reboot.
* We've improved the wander range of brown bears, rogues and bandits within the Wilderness. This should make it easier to use your Dwarf multicannon and/or Ice barrage for some of your Wilderness Slayer tasks.
* Damage in Wintertodt will now visibly interrupt Fletching animations.
* The grey, teal, yellow, purple and red boots are no longer members-only items, for consistency with the gloves from the same Canifis shop. Bring on your best fashionscape!
* The Cemetery Teleport spell no longer pops up its Wilderness warning when clicked unless you're actually able to cast the spell, so misclicks will be less disruptive.
* When using a gold bar on a furnace, you will no longer need to confirm you want to craft a Gold Tiara if the only mould you have on you is a tiara mould.
* A typo has been corrected in the Curse of the Empty Lord miniquest journal.
* A graphical issue with the 10th Birthday Balloons has now been fixed.

